# The source stays private. GitHub mirrors what npm ships, nothing more.
#
# npm serves five files and no source: dist/, LICENSE, README.md,
# package.json. The repo now shows the same set, so the public record and
# the published artifact cannot disagree.
#
# The tokenizer and the abstain rules already moved server-side on 26 Jul,
# so the client holds no verdict logic worth reading. What it does hold is
# every comment explaining WHY: the WSL trap, why { is a keyword prefix,
# the libuv abort, the false positives that cost 270 denials. That is the
# expensive part, and it is not distribution.
src/
